A quick search found this little gem for word frequencies

tr -cs A-Za-z\' '\n' | tr A-Z a-z | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1nr -k2

Running it against the corpus gives the attached frequencies. However don't
use this freq list, as it includes many english words, abbreviations and
author's names. Ideally one would clean the corpus of non-lojban and then
run this script on it.

-- Ross

